Usage:
  lark-cli docs +fetch [flags]

Flags:
      --api-version string      API version (v1|v2) (default "v1")
      --as string               identity type: user | bot (default "user")
      --context-after int       range/keyword/section mode: sibling blocks after match
      --context-before int      range/keyword/section mode: sibling blocks before match
      --doc string              document URL or token
      --dry-run                 print request without executing
      --end-block-id string     range mode: end block id; "-1" = to end of document
      --format string           output format: json (default) | pretty | table | ndjson | csv (default "json")
  -h, --help                    help for +fetch
  -q, --jq string               jq expression to filter JSON output
      --keyword string          keyword mode: search string (case-insensitive); use '|' to match multiple keywords, e.g. 'foo|bar|baz'
      --max-depth int           outline: heading level cap; range/keyword/section: block subtree depth (-1 = unlimited) (default -1)
      --scope string            partial read scope: outline | range | keyword | section (omit to read whole doc) (full|outline|range|keyword|section) (default "full")
      --start-block-id string   range/section mode: start (anchor) block id

Global Flags:
      --profile string   use a specific profile

